-- Birmingham, Jacksonville and Milwaukee now have five or more active rows: published with an intro.
UPDATE "City" SET "published" = 1, "intro" = 'Birmingham''s American mahjong lives in libraries, churches and gardens. O''Neal Library''s Monday meetup plays with the National Mah Jongg League card at a temporary home in Mountain Brook, Riverchase United Methodist Church teaches free lessons on first Thursdays, and Aldridge Gardens in Hoover holds free open play twice a month with a beginner lesson beforehand. Levite JCC also runs open play and a Mahjong 101 series. New players can start with the Riverchase lessons.', "updatedAt" = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE "slug" = 'birmingham' AND "published" = 0;
UPDATE "City" SET "published" = 1, "intro" = 'In Jacksonville, Mahjong Social Club Jax runs American mahjong nights at local restaurants and cafes, including Grazing Parlor in Jacksonville Beach, Trattoria Di Bernardone and Gaa Cafe, with Mahjong 101 lessons and open play. Games use the current National Mah Jongg League card, so bring yours. Popular nights can fill up, so book ahead. If you have never played, start with a Mahjong 101 class at Grazing Parlor.', "updatedAt" = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE "slug" = 'jacksonville' AND "published" = 0;
UPDATE "City" SET "published" = 1, "intro" = 'Milwaukee''s American mahjong includes weekly play at the Harry & Rose Samson Family JCC and at the Whole Foods Market on Prospect Avenue, plus city recreation classes and meet-ups at the Schuetze Recreation Center in Waukesha. Julie Littman of MKE Mahjong teaches National Mah Jongg League rules and runs lessons and parties around the metro. Check each group''s page for the next date. If you are new, ask about a beginner lesson first.', "updatedAt" = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE "slug" = 'milwaukee' AND "published" = 0;
